  "audio_file": "short_sf_energy_rule.mp3",
  "text": "The 1 Energy Regulator Rule for Zero Lag: Slimefun uses graph traversal each tick to distribute Joules. Two regulators in one circuit trigger recursive JVM recalculations. Exactly 1 regulator per circuit = 20.0 flawless TPS. Test it on play.drakescraft.cl!",
  "spoken_text": "Here is the golden engineering rule for zero-lag Slimefun networks: never place two Energy Regulators on the same connected circuit. During every server tick, Slimefun performs a breadth-first search to traverse the network graph and distribute Joules. When multiple regulators share connected cables or machines, the JVM recalculates the graph repeatedly, creating exponential tick lag. Keep exactly one regulator per isolated energy grid for twenty point zero flawless TPS. Play lag-free Slimefun right now on play dot drakescraft dot cl.",
